1. THE WORK

   "The Work" means everything the author created and published in this
   repository: source code, curriculum text and examples (Indonesian and
   English), visual design, documentation, tests, configuration, and the name
   and branding "RanMotion". It also includes contributions accepted into the
   repository (see section 5). It does not include Third-Party Components (see
   section 6).

   "You" means any person or organization using the Work.

2. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   For personal, educational, or evaluation purposes, and not for commercial
   purposes, you may:

   a. view and read the Work;
   b. clone or download it to your own devices;
   c. run it, and modify it, on your own devices to study how it works, to
      learn, or to evaluate the author's skills (for example during hiring or
      portfolio review);
   d. fork it on GitHub, as GitHub's Terms of Service allow, to study it or to
      propose a contribution by pull request. A fork stays under this license;
   e. quote short excerpts with clear credit to the author and a link to this
      repository;
   f. visit and use the version of RanMotion that the author hosts, as
      intended.

3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO WITHOUT PRIOR WRITTEN PERMISSION

   a. Publish, host, deploy, or otherwise make available to others the Work or
      any modified or derived version of it: on a website, web app, hosting
      platform, package registry, mirror, or any repository other than a
      GitHub fork allowed by section 2(d). This includes deploying an
      unmodified or lightly modified copy under another name, domain, or
      account.
   b. Redistribute, sell, rent, lease, or sublicense the Work, or offer it to
      others as a service.
   c. Use the Work commercially, including in paid courses, products, client
